 "accepted_at_0.9": false,
 "verdict": "Not accepted. On the 30 held-out cases at 0.9 it acted on 21 and was wrong on 2: profile-phone (clicked Update while the pre-filled phone field still needed PHONE#1) and support-desc-free (a step that needs free text: free-text probability 0.05, clicked Submit at 0.98). Jev at 0.9 was right on every held-out step it answered and never acted on a free-text step. Design cases at 0.9: 6 of 11 acted, all right.",
 "findings": [
  "The free-text question now trains: training loss reaches its floor (0.1985, the entropy of the 0.95/0.05 targets) by epoch 3-4 in every run, and on unseen generated steps its AUROC is 1.0 for all 12 candidates. The CPU runs never separated it.",
  "Validation from the same generator saturates (1,612-1,619 of 1,619 top choices right; precision 0.996-1.0 at 0.9) and no longer separates candidates; the held-out benchmark does (precision 0.905).",
  "Both held-out errors are situations the generator never produces: a field that is already filled but must be overwritten (profile-phone), and a free-text need stated as 'about <topic>' after a click on another control (support-desc-free). Over-flagging free text on ship-name, ship-addr, ship-continue, mail-to and login-no-forgot costs coverage, not safety.",
  "Confidence is capped by the training targets: chosen-option probability is 0.98 (1 - WRONG_MASS) and free-text 0.05/0.95 on almost every case, so the 0.9 threshold only removes the few cases the model is unsure of.",
  "The runtime restarted after the 16:11 IST snapshot, so all four runs trained a second time (losses differ slightly from the snapshot); the numbers here are from the completed second pass."
 ],
 "caveats": "Synthetic, already-tokenized scenes written by us, for both training and evaluation. One rep per held-out case (Laya is deterministic). Not a field estimate. Weights were not uploaded; the selected checkpoint is on Francis's Drive only."
}
